                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Dilation of the airways leading to more air intake</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Increased heart rate and increased contractility of the heart to supply fresh blood at a rapid pace</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Decreased salivation leading to dry mouth and decreased movement of the GIT leading to possible constipation if the response is long enough.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>A constriction of the 'peripheral' blood vessels (like to the skin, to the GIT) leading to increased blood pressure.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Pupils become very dilated, leading to possible eye pain if the room is brightly lit.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>High levels of glucose because we need instant energy</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NO. There are two types of receptors for adrenaline on the blood vessels. The alpha 1 receptors are on the peripheral blood vessels and they indeed constrict with adrenaline binding. BUT, the diaphram and the big muscles that we need to run away have beta receptors that result in dilation. We want MORE blood to the big muscles.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Indeed, there are two types of receptors for adrenaline on the blood vessels. The alpha 1 receptors are on the peripheral blood vessels and they indeed constrict with adrenaline binding. BUT, the diaphram and the big muscles that we need to run away have beta receptors that result in dilation. We want MORE blood to the big muscles.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Constriction of the blood vessels to the big muscles that we need to run away</div>\n"
                }
