              "question": "<p>For the most part, we can predict what will happen with a sympathetic response if we take each organ and think about it logically. The exception to that is the effect of that response in the urinary system. With a fight or flight response, there are things relaxing and contracting all over the place, but the ultimate response is that \"<strong>we need to flee not wee</strong>\". There is an overall decrease in the ability to urinate. (But in some cases, you will hear about someone who did the opposite during a good fright, because of the complexity of the response at the urinary system.)&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Other organs are much more predictable. Choose the response(s) that you would expect to find in a sympathetic nervous system response:</p>\n"
            },
